---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { ENGINES, ROWS, fmt, cell, cellShort } from '../data/rb';

const DOWNLOAD = 'https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/releases/tag/v0.1.1';

const rows = ROWS.filter(r => r.front);
const rivals = ENGINES.filter(e => e.id !== 'R');
---
<SiteLayout title="Halowin Bubo: a local LLM server for AMD Strix Halo on Windows" description="Halowin Bubo runs Qwen3.8 Flash Next (125B parameters, 6B active) on AMD Strix Halo laptops at about 70 W. Native on Windows, free, OpenAI-compatible.">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <div class="hero-main">
      <span class="eyebrow">v0.1.1 · MIT · Windows 11</span>
      <p class="display">The most intelligence a laptop can fit</p>
      <h1 id="home-title">A local LLM server for AMD Strix Halo, native on Windows</h1>
      <p class="intro">Halowin Bubo runs Qwen3.8 Flash Next on your laptop. The new app helps you download the model, starts it and shows what it uses. Version 0.1.1 reads prompts and writes faster than 0.1.0 and adds support for <a href="https://huggingface.co/ISTA-DASLab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF">ISTA GSQ-RCO</a> derived memory efficient quants without compromising on reasoning quality for lower memory usage enabling more subagents and more context at slightly slower speeds.</p>
      <div class="cta-row"><a class="button" href={DOWNLOAD}>Download v0.1.1 for Windows</a><a class="cta-link" href="/docs/system-setup/">System setup <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <p class="feature-line">OpenAI-compatible API · tool calling · up to 262K context · tested with the Pi coding agent</p>
      <p class="needs">Needs Windows 11 and an AMD Strix Halo machine. Qwen3.8 Flash Next needs 128 GB of memory and about 113 GiB of free disk. Smaller models need less. On a 96 GB machine, use the <a href="/models/">lower-memory build</a>. MIT license. See the <a href="/docs/known-issues/">known issues</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-stats">
      <p class="proof"><strong>Qwen3.8 Flash Next: 125B parameters</strong> (6B active) at <a href="/docs/system-setup/#power-mode">about 70 W</a></p>
      <p class="chart-stat"><span class="chart-num">68.5</span> <span class="chart-unit">tok/s</span></p>
      <p class="chart-claim">writing, in a long agent session at about 70 W</p>
      <p class="chart-stat second"><span class="chart-num">1,384</span> <span class="chart-unit">tok/s</span></p>
      <p class="chart-claim">reading a 32K prompt</p>
      <p class="measure-note">Bubo 0.1.1, same laptop and model file as the table below. <a href="/benchmarks/">Benchmarks <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="versus" aria-labelledby="versus-title">
    <h2 id="versus-title">Faster on the same laptop</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" rowspan="2"><span class="visually-hidden">Workload</span></th>
            <th scope="col" rowspan="2" class="us">Bubo 0.1.1</th>
            <th scope="colgroup" colspan="3" class="group">Bubo is faster than</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            {rivals.map(e => <th scope="col"><a href={e.url}>{e.name}</a><br /><span class="sub">{e.sub}{e.frontSub ? ' · ' + e.frontSub : ''}</span></th>)}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map(r => <tr><th scope="row">{r.front!.label}<span class="sub">{r.front!.what}</span></th><td class="us">{fmt(r.bubo, r.decimals)}</td>{rivals.map(e => <td class="ratio">{cellShort(r[e.id])}</td>)}</tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="measure-note">Same laptop at about 70 W, same model file for every engine. Level means within 3 %. <a href="/benchmarks/">Method and every row <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="news" aria-labelledby="news-title">
    <h2 id="news-title">New in 0.1.1</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>An app.</strong> Pick a model, press Start, and watch memory and requests. Update Bubo with one click.</li>
      <li><strong>Faster.</strong> Mixed work runs up to 11 % faster than 0.1.0, and code edits 10 % faster.</li>
      <li><strong>Memory guard.</strong> Bubo keeps 4 GiB of memory free and turns away a request that does not fit, so the PC keeps running.</li>
      <li><strong>A lower-memory Flash Next.</strong> A build of Qwen3.8 Flash Next with smaller expert weights from ISTA-DASLab’s GSQ-RCO quantization. At the default context it needs about 66 GiB of GPU memory instead of about 91 GiB. It is the build to use on a 96 GB machine. Prose runs at about the same speed; code and agent text at about 0.75 to 0.9 of the standard build. <a href="/models/">Models supported</a></li>
      <li><strong>Eight more models,</strong> 16 to 23 GB each, for machines with less memory: Qwen3.8 27B, Qwen3.6 27B, Cyber-Tiel Coder, Gemma 4 26B and 31B (two builds each) and DiffusionGemma. All take images. <a href="/models/">Models supported</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="home-visual" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <h2 id="start-title">Start in four steps</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="step-head"><span>1. <a href="/docs/install/#prepare-the-machine">Prepare the machine</a>: GPU memory, page file, power mode</span></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-head"><span>2. Download the zip and unzip it</span></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-head"><span>3. Double-click <code>start.cmd</code></span></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-head"><span>4. Approve the download, then press Start</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="measure-note"><a href="/docs/install/">Install guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
  :global(main) { padding-top: 44px; }
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 56px; align-items: start; padding-bottom: 54px; }
  .hero-main { min-width: 0; }
  .display { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4.8vw, 4.2rem); line-height: 1.05; font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 14px 0 12px; max-width: 14em; }
  .proof { margin: 0 0 26px; font-size: 1.25rem; padding-left: 14px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); line-height: 1.35; }
  .proof strong { font-weight: 700; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.7vw, 1.4rem); font-style: normal; color: var(--ink); letter-spacing: 0; margin: 0 0 10px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .hero .intro { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: 0; }
  .feature-line { margin: 18px 0 0; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  .needs { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: .95rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; max-width: 640px; }
  .hero-stats { min-width: 0; padding-top: 6px; }
  .chart-stat { margin: 0; line-height: 1; }
  .chart-stat.second { margin-top: 26px; }
  .chart-num { color: var(--accent); font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 6vw, 5rem); letter-spacing: -.035em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .chart-unit { font-size: 1.4rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .chart-claim { margin: 4px 0 12px; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .versus { padding-top: 6px; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  .versus table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; max-width: 900px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .versus th, .versus td { padding: 11px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.35; vertical-align: top; }
  .versus thead th { font-weight: 400; vertical-align: bottom; }
  .versus th[scope='row'] { text-align: left; font-weight: 400; }
  .versus .sub { display: block; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .versus .us { background: var(--tint); }
  .versus thead .us { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }
  .versus td.us { color: var(--accent); }
  .versus td.ratio { color: var(--accent); white-space: nowrap; }
  .versus thead th.group { text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); }
  .visually-hidden { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; }
  section + section { margin-top: 40px; }
  .news ul { max-width: 760px; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .news li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .home-visual { margin-top: 56px; }
  .steps { max-width: 820px; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .step { min-width: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--wash); }
  .step-head { padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  code { font: .92em var(--mono); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 36px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .versus th, .versus td { padding: 9px 8px; font-size: .95rem; }
    .versus .sub { font-size: .75rem; }
  }
</style>
